# Grading Worksheet

**F1 Core loop**: single `S` object; `mkRng`/`R()` seeded PRNG used everywhere (no `Math.random`); `endTurn()`→`runTurn()` calls phases in fixed documented order. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: `genMap(seed)` builds 64-tile grid from seeded rng; `tryBuild` checks `d.terr.includes(s.map[i])`; `adjCount()` used in condenser/greenhouse/forge production formulas, changing real yield numbers. Score 2.

**F3 Economy**: chains sifter(ash→soil)→greenhouse(soil+water→food), mine(ore)→forge(ore+power→metal)→workshop(metal+power→parts); `caps()`+`addRes()` clamp and log overflow. Score 2.

**F4 Population**: colonist records `{skill,xp,fatigue,morale,job,b}`; `workerMult()` reads `c.skill`/`c.fatigue` inside `production()`. Score 2.

**F5 Needs**: `needsPhase()` deducts food/water per pop; shortage → `dm-=12/-10` into `c.morale`; `workerMult` reads morale into output; positive `dm` allows gradual recovery. Score 2.

**F6 Research**: 10 nodes; `tryResearch` enforces `node.req.every(has)`; costs deducted via `spend`; each id (`filters`,`drip`,`bore`,`turbine`,`heatx`,`depots`,`barter`,`shield`,`salvage`,`medbay`) is read via `has()` in production/caps/priceOf/stormPhase/build-req. Score 2.

**F7 Events**: 12 events in `EVENTS`; weighted roll in `eventsPhase()`; 6 events have 2-3 choices with distinct `apply()` state mutations; `s.cds[id]=EVENT_COOLDOWN` filters pool. Score 2.

**F8 Trade**: `priceOf()` reads `s.res[g]/cap` (scarcity) and `s.drift[g]` (random walk in `caravanPhase`); `cv.inv[g]` limited and decremented; `tradeDeal` handles both buy/sell. Score 2.

**F9 Hazard**: `stormPhase()` fires every 8 turns, `sev=1+floor(turn/20)`; `production()` checks `b.hp<50`(half)/`<=0`(disabled); `shield` research + `wallCount()` reduce `mit`; `tryRepair` spends parts+metal+colonist fatigue, resets hp. Score 2.

**F10 Save/load**: `exportSave()` → textarea; `importSave()` validates required fields/types, returns descriptive error strings shown in `#saveerr`. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions**: `checkEnd()` — lose (`colonists.length===0`), win (`turn>=60 && pop>=12 && !shortage`), both reachable (starvation test proves lose path); `score()` combines pop/research/turns/stockpile; `renderModal()` renders summary table. Score 2.

**F12 UI**: `switchTab()` wired to buttons; `logMsg` stores `s.turn`, shown as `T${e.t}`; extensive `title=` tooltips with formulas; Space/1-5 keydown handlers; `@media(max-width:420px)` layout rules. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel**: `runTests()` asserts real invariants (cap respect, prereq enforcement, save round-trip hash, starvation departure); `runBench()` runs 200 headless `greedyTurn()` turns via swapped `S`, prints `stateHash()`. Score 2.

**G1**: `has(s,"filters")` etc. read directly inside `production()`'s per-building formulas, applied every turn, visible in `b.note`. Score 4.

**G2**: `needsPhase` writes `c.morale` from shortfall; `workerMult(s,c,d)` reads `c.morale` to scale `m`, consumed by `production()` every turn; visible via morale bar/tile note. Score 4.

**G3**: `stormPhase` sets `b.hp`; `production` checks `b.hp<50/<=0`; `tryRepair` spends `{parts:2,metal:1}`+colonist fatigue and resets `hp=100`, restoring output next turn. Score 4.

**G4**: `priceOf()` reads `s.res[g]` scarcity and `s.drift[g]` (updated every turn in `caravanPhase`), consumed in both buy/sell paths and Trade tab display. Score 4.

**G5**: `refugees`/`thieves` choice branches each write distinct `s.colonists`/`s.res` mutations (not just `logMsg`), verified across 6 choice-events. Score 4.

